# Dropped into /portfolio-a/ as .htaccess by .github/workflows/preview.yml, and
# by nothing else — deploy.yml never copies it, so the live page at /portfolio/
# keeps its own indexing. This folder is a near-duplicate of that page, and two
# indexable copies of the same portfolio means a search engine picks one of
# them, with no say from us about which.
#
# X-Robots-Tag rather than a meta tag, because the page itself is one file
# serving both folders and a meta noindex in it would take the live page down
# with it. The header does the same job from outside the document, and it
# covers the assets too.
#
# Guarded: this host has mod_headers, but an .htaccess naming a module that is
# not loaded is a 500 on the whole directory, and a preview that 500s is worse
# than one that gets indexed.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header always set X-Robots-Tag "noindex, nofollow"
</IfModule>
